"""A short review guide and balanced file assignments; sends nothing to teammates."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];OUT=ROOT/'Dance_Overnight';D=OUT/'CVAT_Review';manifest=json.loads((D/'development/manifest.json').read_text());training=[r for r in manifest if r['split']=='train'];validation=[r for r in manifest if r['split']=='val'];assignments={f'Teammate {x}':training[i::3]+validation[i::3] for i,x in enumerate('ABC')}
(D/'review_assignments.json').write_text(json.dumps(assignments,indent=2))
tables=''.join(f'<details><summary>{html.escape(name)} · 20 training + {sum(r["split"]=="val" for r in rows)} validation frames</summary><p><a href="teammate_{name[-1]}/images.zip">Your image ZIP</a> · <a href="teammate_{name[-1]}/annotations.xml">Your starter XML</a></p><p class="files">'+', '.join(html.escape(r['filename'])+' ['+r['split']+']' for r in rows)+'</p></details>' for name,rows in assignments.items())
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dance labels · team review guide</title>
<style>body{margin:0;background:#f3f4f0;color:#253c35;font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1060px;margin:auto;padding:48px 28px 80px}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.15;margin:12px 0 18px}h2{font-size:25px;margin-top:40px}a{color:#16715e}p{max-width:850px}img{width:100%;border-radius:14px}small,.muted{color:#66766f}.tag{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#16715e}.note{padding:20px 24px;border-left:4px solid #b48a40;background:#fffaf0;border-radius:4px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:white}td,th{padding:13px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #e2e8e1}th{font-size:14px}details{padding:14px 18px;background:white;margin:10px 0;border-radius:10px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}.files{font-size:13px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}li{margin:9px 0}code{background:#e7ebe4;padding:2px 5px;border-radius:4px;font-size:.88em}</style>
<main><div class="tag">Dance stage mapping · annotation review</div><h1>One dancer. One support point.<br>A clear visibility label.</h1>
<p>Review the prepared examples before labeling more frames. These points are assistant visual estimates and need a human check. The model learns from individual dancer crops, so one frame can provide around twenty training examples.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>This is a review pack, not a request to label the whole video.</strong> The main training set uses 56 source frames. Nine additional development frames are reserved for validation. The separate nine-frame and seven-frame evaluation packs stay outside training. The supplemental ending folder is a later development experiment and is not part of the assignments below.</div>
<h2>1. Open the prepared annotations</h2><ol><li>Create an image annotation task in CVAT with the two labels in <a href="labels_schema.json">labels_schema.json</a>: <code>dancer</code> rectangles and <code>floor_support</code> points.</li><li>Upload <a href="development/images.zip">development/images.zip</a>. Then import <a href="development/annotations.xml">annotations.xml</a> using <strong>CVAT for images 1.1</strong>.</li><li>Open the job and review your assigned filenames below. Keep <code>sample_split</code> unchanged.</li></ol>
<h2>2. Check the box, then the contact</h2><p>These are support-crop examples, not a complete detector-label set. The review copy includes several corrected duplicate/missing boxes found after the frozen experiments; those corrections have not changed the reported scores.</p><p>The box covers the dancer’s visible body, including visible arms and legs. Exclude shadows, reflections and neighboring bodies where possible. When people overlap, make sure the box belongs to the intended person. Add missed distinguishable dancers; remove duplicate boxes.</p>
<p>Place the support point at the center of the primary floor contacts. It is a point on the floor, not the body center or an ankle floating above the floor. A planted foot means the sole contact, not its shadow.</p>
<a href="../figures/label_examples.jpg"><img src="../figures/label_examples.jpg" alt="Source-image examples showing feet, knees, mixed support, seated contact, hands, hidden, airborne and uncertain labels"></a>
<table><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>What to label</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>One or two planted feet</td><td>The sole planted foot, or the midpoint between the two supporting feet.</td></tr><tr><td>Kneeling</td><td>The midpoint of clearly supporting knees. Use the primary lower-body supports even if hands also touch the floor.</td></tr><tr><td>One knee and one foot</td><td>The midpoint of the grounded knee and planted foot. Set <code>support_type=mixed_knee_foot</code>.</td></tr><tr><td>Sitting / hands-only support</td><td>The visible seat contact, or the midpoint of supporting palms when the hands alone support the dancer.</td></tr><tr><td>Supporting region hidden</td><td><code>contact=hidden</code>; no support point. Do not place a guessed point behind another person.</td></tr><tr><td>Clearly airborne</td><td><code>contact=airborne</code>; no support point.</td></tr><tr><td>Too blurred or ambiguous</td><td><code>contact=uncertain</code>; no support point. These examples are excluded from clean supervised training.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><strong>Use the <code>contact</code> attribute for floor visibility.</strong> The rectangle’s “occluded” checkbox is not a substitute. A visible contact has exactly one point. Hidden, airborne and uncertain contacts have none.</p>
<h2>3. Keep each box and point linked</h2><p>The prepared box and point share an <code>instance_id</code> and group. Keep them together when editing. For a newly added dancer, use a new positive instance ID and give its point the same ID. These sparse training images need IDs within each image; you do not need to trace choreography-long identities for this support model.</p>
<p>The stage grid is a separate calibration. Do not redraw it per dancer or per training frame. It stays fixed while the camera is fixed; actual stage measurements would be needed to report meters.</p>
<h2>4. Review assignments</h2><p>Training frames are distributed across the timeline. Validation remains separate. The filenames below identify the exact images; avoid editing a teammate’s assigned frames at the same time.</p>'''+tables+'''
<h2>5. Export and validate</h2><p>Export as <strong>CVAT for images 1.1</strong>. Keep the original export and save the reviewer’s name and date. The supplied converter checks missing points, duplicate IDs and split attributes:</p><pre><code>python code/import_cvat_review.py annotations.xml reviewed_labels.json</code></pre><p class="muted">Run from the folder containing the supplied code folder. The converter creates a new revision and never overwrites the frozen training manifests. Human corrections should be reviewed before a new training run. This pack has been checked by XML round-trip; it has not been uploaded into your CVAT account during the overnight experiment.</p></main></html>'''
repeat=OUT/'label_repeatability/results.json'
if repeat.exists():
    r=json.loads(repeat.read_text());flags=r['different_contact_status'];items=''.join(f"<li>Source frame <strong>{o['source_frame']}</strong>, instance <strong>{o['instance_id']}</strong>: {o['original_contact']} on the first pass, {o['repeat_contact']} on the second. Review the full body and supporting region.</li>" for o in flags)
    page=page.replace('<h2>4. Review assignments</h2>',f'<h2>Priority checks from the repeat review</h2><p>Re-marking 20 training crops without seeing the old points gave a median difference of {r["median_pixel_difference"]:.1f} source pixels among contacts marked visible both times. This is not an independent human audit. Resolve these ambiguous contacts first; use uncertain when the image does not support a clear answer.</p><ul>{items}</ul><p>The review flags do not change frozen training labels or scores. All three flagged source frames are included in the main review task.</p><h2>4. Review assignments</h2>')
page=page.replace('The main training set uses 56 source frames. Nine additional development frames are reserved for validation. The separate nine-frame and seven-frame evaluation packs stay outside training. The supplemental ending folder is a later development experiment and is not part of the assignments below.','The main task now combines 60 training frames and 11 separate validation frames. Training is split 20 / 20 / 20. The three reserved evaluation folders stay outside training. The supplemental_ending folder is an earlier separate export of six images already included in the main task; do not import those images twice.')
page=page.replace('The main task now combines 60 training frames and 11 separate validation frames. Training is split 20 / 20 / 20.','The master contains 60 training frames and 11 separate validation frames. Each teammate receives a separate task pack: 20 training frames plus 4 / 4 / 3 validation frames. The three packs have no overlapping images.')
page=page.replace('Upload <a href="development/images.zip">development/images.zip</a>. Then import <a href="development/annotations.xml">annotations.xml</a> using <strong>CVAT for images 1.1</strong>.','Choose your A, B or C pack below. Upload its <strong>images.zip</strong>, then import its matching <strong>annotations.xml</strong> using <strong>CVAT for images 1.1</strong>. Each teammate creates a separate task; do not edit the same job concurrently.')
page=page.replace('Training frames are distributed across the timeline. Validation remains separate. The filenames below identify the exact images; avoid editing a teammate’s assigned frames at the same time.','Training frames are distributed across the timeline. Validation images keep their val tags and stay out of training. Each pack is disjoint. The development folder is the combined master, for a single reviewer or archive; use the three teammate packs for parallel work.')
page=page.replace('Human corrections should be reviewed before a new training run.','After all three exports pass, combine them with <code>python code/merge_review_exports.py combined_review.json A.json B.json C.json</code>. Human corrections should be reviewed before a new training run.')
page=page.replace('<h2>3. Keep each box and point linked</h2>','<p>For a two-foot or two-knee midpoint, both primary supports must be clear. Use a single support only when the other limb is clearly lifted. If a primary support is hidden by another dancer, the person’s own body, or clothing that prevents you locating it, mark hidden. If you cannot tell which supports carry the dancer, mark uncertain. Do not use a shadow as a contact.</p><h2>3. Keep each box and point linked</h2>')
page=page.replace('</main></html>', '<h2>After the human review</h2><p>The full experiment package can turn the merged revision into a new training manifest and train under a new run name. Follow REPRODUCE.txt. The small labeling ZIP is for review and export; it does not contain the GPU training environment.</p></main></html>')
page=page.replace('<h2>1. Open the prepared annotations</h2>', '<h2>1. Open the prepared annotations</h2><p>On the CVAT Tasks page, choose + → Create new task. Leave Project empty for a standalone task. In the labels editor, use Raw and paste the supplied labels_schema.json; it creates both shapes and the attribute menus. See the <a href="https://docs.cvat.ai/docs/workspace/tasks-page/">official task setup guide</a>.</p>')
page=page.replace('<h2>3. Keep each box and point linked</h2>', '<p>Set contact, support_type and sample_split on the dancer rectangle. The point only needs its matching instance_id. Use the dropdowns; a newly drawn rectangle starts as uncertain, with sample_split unset. Set its split to match the other dancers in that image. The export check will reject an unset split or a visible point without a support type.</p><h2>3. Keep each box and point linked</h2>')
(D/'GUIDE.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8');print('Guide and training-frame assignments written:',{k:len(v) for k,v in assignments.items()})
